WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.629 --> 00:00:19.492
watched as the younger girls in the junior division pushed off, one by one.

2
00:00:22.314 --> 00:00:28.198
The riders started racing at thirty-second intervals, which meant that several riders shared the track at one time.

3
00:00:29.118 --> 00:00:33.601
As each rider rolled over the finish line, Coach Adams recorded his or her time.

4
00:00:35.682 --> 00:00:39.644
Finally only Quinn and Riley were left in the girls' junior division.

5
00:00:40.404 --> 00:00:44.766
The two girls mounted their bikes and waited for the whistle to signal Quinn's start.

6
00:00:44.786 --> 00:00:49.568
"Good luck," Quinn muttered.

7
00:00:49.588 --> 00:00:52.490
"Thanks," Riley said with a nod.

8
00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:53.610
"You too."

9
00:00:54.571 --> 00:00:57.472
The whistle blew, and Quinn dashed down the trail.

10
00:01:00.188 --> 00:01:04.230
Riley closed her eyes and breathed slowly, waiting for the next whistle.

11
00:01:08.653 --> 00:01:10.974
"I can do this," she told herself.

12
00:01:10.994 --> 00:01:14.876
"Wherever the brain goes, the body follows."

13
00:01:16.197 --> 00:01:20.359
She opened her eyes and was surprised to feel calm and in control.

14
00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:24.261
She adjusted her helmet and clipped her shoes into the pedals.

15
00:01:26.983 --> 00:01:28.544
Then the whistle sounded again.

16
00:01:31.188 --> 00:01:31.768
"My turn!"

17
00:01:32.289 --> 00:01:32.929
Riley thought.

18
00:01:33.509 --> 00:01:35.950
With one strong push, she burst down the track.

19
00:01:38.711 --> 00:01:41.552
Riley pumped the bike pedals hard, increasing her speed.

20
00:01:42.193 --> 00:01:47.235
She was glad to see that the dirt track was soft but not muddy She took the first

21
00:01:47.295 --> 00:01:49.456
turn easily, leaning into the curve.

22
00:01:50.636 --> 00:01:54.158
After the second curve, the last few jitters seemed to leave her body.

23
00:01:55.938 --> 00:01:57.099
The first jump appeared.

24
00:01:57.699 --> 00:01:59.720
Riley pumped harder and stood up in the saddle.

25
00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:08.043
She bent over the handlebars and easily sailed over the jump, her mind focused on maintaining her weight

26
00:02:08.083 --> 00:02:09.104
and balance in the air.

27
00:02:10.644 --> 00:02:13.486
Both tires hit the ground together, and she sped off.

28
00:02:16.728 --> 00:02:17.708
"Smooth jump!"

29
00:02:18.148 --> 00:02:19.109
she thought with relief.

30
00:02:19.829 --> 00:02:22.291
Now she was actually having fun on the track!

31
00:02:23.711 --> 00:02:25.732
She shifted gears again and sped up.

32
00:02:29.094 --> 00:02:32.076
Soon the bike's speedometer read 12 miles per hour.

33
00:02:33.144 --> 00:02:34.545
"Perfect!" she thought.

34
00:02:35.045 --> 00:02:37.666
The second jump was coming, and she knew she could take it.

35
00:02:38.547 --> 00:02:45.351
The steps felt almost effortless as she performed them: speed up, stop pedaling, lift the bike, balance and

36
00:02:45.391 --> 00:02:47.011
stay airborne, and land.

37
00:02:54.455 --> 00:02:55.016
I made it!"

38
00:02:55.716 --> 00:02:56.837
Riley thought happily.

39
00:02:58.498 --> 00:03:00.319
Suddenly she heard the crowd gasp.

40
00:03:00.339 --> 00:03:02.640
"Was that for Quinn?"

41
00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:04.120
Riley wondered.

42
00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:05.621
"Did something happen?"

43
00:03:06.781 --> 00:03:09.182
There was no sign of Quinn, so there was no way to know.

44
00:03:09.202 --> 00:03:13.704
Riley pumped harder, accelerating back up to 12 miles per hour.

45
00:03:16.906 --> 00:03:20.987
Riley was so focused on regaining speed that she forgot where she was on the track.

46
00:03:21.928 --> 00:03:26.609
After she took the next curve, she realized that another jump was at the end of the straightaway.

47
00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:32.292
It looked like a tricky one, with a mud pit below and a landing ramp a little off

48
00:03:32.352 --> 00:03:34.685
center. Riley gulped.

49
00:03:34.705 --> 00:03:37.287
"Uh-oh," she thought.

50
00:03:37.307 --> 00:03:39.968
"This is the jump where Jordan crashed."

51
00:03:41.509 --> 00:03:44.792
Just then Riley spotted motion on the trail ahead of her.

52
00:03:45.532 --> 00:03:48.274
It was Quinn, racing madly toward the jump.

53
00:03:51.977 --> 00:03:53.658
strange," Riley thought.

54
00:03:53.678 --> 00:03:55.859
"Quinn should be farther ahead of me."

55
00:03:57.140 --> 00:03:59.102
She remembered the gasps from the crowd.

56
00:03:59.762 --> 00:04:02.084
Maybe something had happened to Quinn on the track.

57
00:04:03.188 --> 00:04:05.630
Riley knew she should be focused on her own ride.

58
00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:09.734
But she kept her eyes glued to Quinn as the other girl barreled toward the jump.

59
00:04:10.754 --> 00:04:14.718
Quinn's head was down, and she didn't appear to notice the jump coming at her.

60
00:04:14.738 --> 00:04:16.900
"Look up, look up!"

61
00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:18.121
Riley thought.

62
00:04:18.861 --> 00:04:21.123
At the last minute Riley saw her look up.

63
00:04:22.424 --> 00:04:26.348
But by now Quinn was going too fast to adjust her speed or her balance.

64
00:04:29.951 --> 00:04:34.173
Riley came to a full stop, watching anxiously as Quinn flew over the jump.

65
00:04:35.813 --> 00:04:39.174
Quinn's front tire dipped dangerously lower than the back tire.

66
00:04:40.034 --> 00:04:45.736
Quinn frantically tried to regain her balance, pulling up on the handlebars to straighten the wheels before landing.

67
00:04:46.956 --> 00:04:49.337
"She's not going to make it," Riley thought.

68
00:04:49.357 --> 00:04:51.217
"She's going to crash."

69
00:04:52.338 --> 00:04:57.439
Thud! Quinn's bike came down and hit the edge of the landing ramp with a sickening sound.

70
00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:03.241
The bike flipped, sending Quinn flying over the handlebars.

71
00:05:04.342 --> 00:05:05.402
The crowd gasped.

72
00:05:06.903 --> 00:05:11.925
Riley cringed, bracing herself to see Quinn break her fall improperly, with her hands.

73
00:05:11.945 --> 00:05:14.887
"Here it comes," she murmured.

74
00:05:16.608 --> 00:05:20.669
Instead Quinn tucked her arms into her sides and rolled onto the ground.

75
00:05:22.810 --> 00:05:25.672
The bike bounced away from her, splashing into the mud pit.

76
00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:33.445
The crowd cheered as Quinn quickly jumped up, covered in mud, and grabbed her bike.

77
00:05:37.428 --> 00:05:40.350
Just then Quinn looked up and spotted Riley watching her.

78
00:05:41.151 --> 00:05:44.334
Quinn flashed Riley a determined look as she jumped on her bike.

79
00:05:45.895 --> 00:05:49.578
With one mad push, Quinn got back on the trail and took off.

80
00:05:52.861 --> 00:05:58.893
Riley was so relieved that Quinn wasn't injured, it took her a second to realize that she herself

81
00:05:58.933 --> 00:05:59.993
had come to a stop.

82
00:06:00.013 --> 00:06:04.355
"Ack!" Riley cried as she began pedaling again.

83
00:06:04.375 --> 00:06:09.497
"You're not going to beat me, Quinn Evans!"

84
00:06:10.158 --> 00:06:11.418
She raced toward the jump.

85
00:06:12.679 --> 00:06:17.420
As Riley approached the jump, she saw that Quinn's spill had churned up the soft dirt on the

86
00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:18.021
jump ramp.

87
00:06:19.101 --> 00:06:23.323
Quinn's fall had also taken a big chunk of dirt out of the edge of the landing ramp.

88
00:06:24.203 --> 00:06:29.709
Even before she reached the jump, Riley knew her tires wouldn't have enough traction to hold the landing.

89
00:06:30.629 --> 00:06:33.350
Panic washed over her like cold water.

90
00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:38.512
"No!" Riley yelled, gritting her teeth and gripping the handlebars.

91
00:06:39.712 --> 00:06:43.013
She couldn't lose this race—or her spot on the team.

92
00:06:44.733 --> 00:06:46.474
She pedaled hard and hit the jump.

93
00:06:49.595 --> 00:06:53.696
Her back tire skidded in the soft dirt, but the bike lifted into the air.

94
00:06:54.832 --> 00:06:59.576
Riley rose up, up, over the mud pit, struggling to keep her balance.

95
00:07:00.236 --> 00:07:02.478
Then she braced for the impact of the landing.

96
00:07:03.319 --> 00:07:07.942
The front wheel landed perfectly, but the back wheel barely cleared the edge of the ramp.

97
00:07:09.884 --> 00:07:13.346
As her body flew off the bike, Riley closed her eyes.

98
00:07:14.027 --> 00:07:16.028
She tucked her arms in and bent her head.

99
00:07:17.029 --> 00:07:20.632
She hit the ground hard, sliding through the dirt and right off the trail.

100
00:07:23.864 --> 00:07:26.306
"Ouch!" Riley cried as pain shot through her shoulder.

101
00:07:26.827 --> 00:07:28.748
She rolled to a stop, breathing heavily.

102
00:07:33.792 --> 00:07:38.196
She waited for more pain, but to her surprise, only her shoulder ached.

103
00:07:38.216 --> 00:07:40.618
"I'm okay!"

104
00:07:41.098 --> 00:07:41.859
she told herself.

105
00:07:42.339 --> 00:07:43.460
"I'm still in this race!"

106
00:07:44.261 --> 00:07:47.143
She jumped up, her eyes scanning the mud pit for her bike.

107
00:07:49.565 --> 00:07:54.445
Riley yanked her bike out of the mud pit and jumped back on, flying down the track.

108
00:07:59.428 --> 00:08:00.429
she reminded herself.

109
00:08:00.449 --> 00:08:02.290
"Eyes on the track."

110
00:08:03.430 --> 00:08:09.314
She had lost a lot of time, but maybe, with determination and focus, she could still win the

111
00:08:09.374 --> 00:08:09.674
race.
